# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data (872 MB) -- deliberately NOT tracked.
#
# Everything under data/ is either a user-supplied input or a derived artefact
# that scripts/00_acquire.py and scripts/01_build_db.py rebuild from scratch:
#
#   Ecomics.*.{txt,csv}   the published release (259 MB), from the Ecomics
#                         Dropbox linked at http://prokaryomics.com/download
#   external/             scraped + downloaded resources (189 MB)
#   ecomics.db            the built SQLite compendium (347 MB)
#   parquet/              wide matrices mirrored for fast loading (78 MB)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
data.zip

# Large or regenerable outputs. The reproduction table and per-layer metrics
# ARE tracked -- they are the result of record.
results/*.npz
results/*.log
results/*.png

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In the working
# Code not reachable from scripts/ -- kept locally, not published.
#
#   plots.py, figures/   the figure atlas. Its own entry point,
#                        scripts/15_figures.py, was never written, so the
#                        registry has no caller. ~2,375 lines.
#   moma/{_lasso,fluxome,metabolome,phenome,proteome}.py
#                        the four omics layers beyond the transcriptome, i.e.
#                        the rest of the paper's cascade. scripts/03 imports
#                        only TranscriptomeModule. ~1,607 lines.
#
# moma/__init__.py stays tracked: it re-exports only transcriptome, and Python
# executes it on any `ecomics.moma.*` import.
#
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
ecomics/plots.py
ecomics/figures/
ecomics/moma/_lasso.py
ecomics/moma/fluxome.py
ecomics/moma/metabolome.py
ecomics/moma/phenome.py
ecomics/moma/proteome.py

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
venv/
.venv/

# R
.Rhistory
.RData

